# Always deploy the public site

`git push` updates GitHub only. Vercel Git auto-deploy is off on purpose. Hobby is 100 deploys/day and ignored Git builds still count.

If you changed anything the browser loads from epsynapse.com, the task is not finished until you run a production deploy and confirm the live page.

## When this applies

Run `npm run deploy:web` after commit + push if you touched any of:

- `index.html`, `agent.html`, `favicon.svg`
- `styles.css`, `app.js`, `chatbot.js`, `liquid-glass.js`, `theme-orb.js`
- `runtime-config.json`, `vercel.json`
- any other root static file Vercel serves

Skip only for Mac / agent trees: `server/**`, `docs/`, `deploy/`, `.cursor/`, `ideas.md`, `AGENTS.md`.

## How

From the repo root, on `main`, after `git push origin main`:

```bash
npm run deploy:web
```

That is `scripts/deploy-web.sh` → `npx vercel deploy --prod --yes --scope jype1`. It loads `~/.config/jype/vercel.env` when `VERCEL_TOKEN` is unset, because the default CLI login on this Mac cannot see team `jype1`. Then hit https://epsynapse.com and confirm it is 200 with the new content.

Do not run `vercel git connect`. Do not invent a second host. If the script still cannot see `jype1`, stop and say so.
